details:
While building a world for VRC, i encountered a strange situation in which a behavior that worked perfectly fine within the unity editor failed to work in a built world. After a few days of testing, I discovered that the issue was with the layermask filter in the following raycast check:

if (Physics.Raycast(position, direction, out hit, distance, layermask))

Ive tried using Layermask.GetMask() as well as using the actual integer of the layer i wanted to target, but both failed to work inside of VRChat.

The only workaround Ive found to get around this is to perform the Raycast check without the layermask filter and then check it afterwords i.e.

if (Physics.Raycast(position, direction, out hit, distance, layermask))

    if(hit.collider.gameObject.layer == <layer>)

Although,  this solution has led to a problem with other colliders getting in the way and player colliders throwing errors when trying to grab their gameObject component.
